  "description": "PERWAN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C65 H133 Fe7 Gd4 N7 O44 1+,N1 O3 1-,3.5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 29 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.934-3.965 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.83-134.95°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C65H133Fe7N7O44Gd4·NO3·3.5(C2H3N). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 tea (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 Htea (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 7 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Fe(III), Gd(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
